<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#AnalogicalMapping> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Metaphorical and Analogical Mapping elements from the image. Metaphorical and Analogical Mapping includes: symbolic representations, analogical elements, metaphorical connections, symbolic mappings, figurative elements, and analogical relationships. For each metaphorical element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'fire_metaphor', 'smile_analogy'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the fire metaphor', 'the smile analogy'), 3) A brief description of the metaphorical or analogical meaning. Focus on how one element represents or symbolizes another concept. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"fire_metaphor\", \"label\": \"the fire metaphor\", \"description\": \"The burning house serves as a metaphor for chaos or destruction, contrasting with the girl's calm expression\"}"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#contrast_between_activity_and_rest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "temporal & activity markers"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#horizontallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#objectEmbeddedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text naturally appearing on clothing, objects, and surfaces within meme scenes"@en .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b20 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b21 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perspectivallyContradicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates two dimensions offering different viewpoints on another dimension in memes, e.g. same visual content from different perspectives"@en .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b44 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dramaticallyIronicalTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates one dimension revealing information another dimension does not provide in memes, e.g. text revealing information visuals don't show"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#mudding> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#text_overlay> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#top_text> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "white bold text reading 'when you want to nap' positioned at the top of the image."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#assertion_about_01423> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#mudding> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#white_sheets> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "White sheets cover the bed, appearing rumpled and slightly disheveled, indicating recent use or relaxation. The sheets are smooth and appear to be made of cotton or a similar material."@en .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b76 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b77 .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b47 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b48 .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b99 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme targets individuals who engage in physically demanding outdoor activities like mudding, as the text explicitly references 'after a long day of mudding,' which is a common recreational pursuit for off-road enthusiasts, truckers, or adventure seekers. The visual of restful intimacy after exertion is relatable to this community."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualCompositionCompliant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Typography that conforms to and enhances the geometric structure of memes"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#assertion_about_01423> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#physical_exertion> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#comparativelyPositionedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comparatively positioned to"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#superimposedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b103 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#intimate_posture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An intimate posture refers to physical positioning that suggests closeness, affection, or romantic connection between two people. In the context of the meme, the posture of the two individuals lying together on the bed is interpreted as intimate, which reinforces the idea of restful companionship after physical exertion. The background knowledge required to understand the meme is that such postures are culturally associated with romantic or affectionate relationships, which adds to the humor of the contrast with 'mudding'."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#mudding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mudding is a recreational activity involving driving or riding vehicles through muddy terrain, often for fun or as part of off-road sports. It is physically demanding and typically results in dirty, muddy clothing and skin. The term is commonly associated with outdoor enthusiasts, truckers, or people who enjoy rugged, adventurous activities. The background knowledge required to understand the meme is that 'mudding' implies a physically exhausting and messy activity, which contrasts humorously with the image of restful intimacy."@en .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b59 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b60 .
