<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundPreservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text placed only over neutral areas to preserve important visual content in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#text_overlay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "White text with a black outline is overlaid on the image. The top text reads 'when you want to nap' and the bottom text reads 'after a long day of mudding.' The text is centered and uses a bold, sans-serif font, creating a humorous and relatable contrast with the visual of rest."@en .
