<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual material of two nude individuals in an intimate, restful posture on a bed is mapped onto the textual concept of 'when you want to nap after a long day of mudding'. The image visually represents the state of rest and intimacy that is the desired outcome after the implied physical labor of 'mudding'. The text explicitly labels this visual state as the desired result of the activity mentioned."@en .
_:n04d72e1a0fc345aa8e9e64a712e4da96b26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Scene is the interpretation of a composition of visual material entities that are related to each other in a specific way. It includes: visual elements participating in the scene, spatial arrangements, element positioning, scene understanding, layout structures, and spatial relationships."@en .
