<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual and textual elements that represent the ideal outcome of a physically demanding activity — namely, the restful, intimate, and comfortable state depicted in the image and described by the text 'when you want to nap after a long day of mudding'. The use of 'you' in the text directly addresses the viewer, inviting them to identify with the scenario. The user is thus projected onto the scene of restful intimacy and the concept of napping as a reward for hard work."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#backgroundPreserving> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relationIndex> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#causallyRelatedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
